// W2F display text (English). Loaded next to champions.json; the server sends it in the `catalog` message (`text.entries`) so a client can build its
// localisation table (in Unreal: a String Table, key -> text) without hard-coding any wording.
//
// Keys (a flat map, dotted; ids are the ids in the data files, so keys survive renames):
//   champion.<id>.name / .title / .desc              every champion, summon and monster has a name; title and desc are optional
//   champion.<id>.ability.name / .ability.desc       for champions with an active ability
//   champion.<id>.passive.name / .passive.desc       for champions with a passive
//   trait.<id>.name / .tagline / .bp<count>          one bp<count> per breakpoint of the trait (bp3, bp6 ...)
//   item.<id>.name / .desc                           every item
//   gift.<id>.name / .desc                           every Mother Nature gift
// "a/b/c" in a text means the value at 1 / 2 / 3 stars.  The tests require an entry for everything above and that each name equals the name in the data.
// The numbers in the descriptions are written by hand: after a balance change to a champion, trait or item, update its sentence here.
